1
00:00:00,819 --> 00:00:03,923
On day 271, nobody opens the gate.

2
00:00:03,923 --> 00:00:06,564
The knock does not come again.

3
00:00:06,564 --> 00:00:09,111
For a long time, there is only the

4
00:00:09,111 --> 00:00:10,895
torch beam lying across the vent grille

5
00:00:10,895 --> 00:00:12,805
like a finger on your lips,

6
00:00:12,805 --> 00:00:15,997
and four people in the dark trying not to breathe.

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,359
Your name is Patch.

8
00:00:18,359 --> 00:00:19,567
Two hundred and seventy days ago,

9
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:21,724
you were waiting for a bus.

10
00:00:21,724 --> 00:00:24,451
Since then, you have lived under a

11
00:00:24,451 --> 00:00:25,492
bus depot with Nora,

12
00:00:25,492 --> 00:00:28,972
who used to clean it, Wes, who used to live on a roof,

13
00:00:28,972 --> 00:00:31,097
and Vera, who drove the last bus

14
00:00:31,097 --> 00:00:33,464
out of your yard, and a month ago drove

15
00:00:33,464 --> 00:00:35,478
a few thousand of the dead into a

16
00:00:35,478 --> 00:00:37,919
gravel pit and shut a gate behind them.

17
00:00:38,229 --> 00:00:40,404
You know everything about the dead.

18
00:00:40,404 --> 00:00:41,310
How they walk.

19
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:42,878
What they follow.

20
00:00:42,878 --> 00:00:43,816
Where they stop.

21
00:00:43,816 --> 00:00:45,472
You know nothing at all about

22
00:00:45,472 --> 00:00:47,829
whoever is standing at your gate.

23
00:00:47,829 --> 00:00:49,648
Then a voice comes over the wall.

24
00:00:49,648 --> 00:00:50,857
A woman's voice.

25
00:00:51,294 --> 00:00:52,016
Not loud.

26
00:00:52,016 --> 00:00:53,749
Not whispering either.

27
00:00:53,749 --> 00:00:55,535
"We're not dead," she says.

28
00:00:55,535 --> 00:00:57,804
"And we're not here to take anything.

29
00:00:57,804 --> 00:00:59,305
Where we come from,

30
00:00:59,305 --> 00:01:01,160
two knocks means that."

31
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:03,084
Nora looks at you.

32
00:01:03,084 --> 00:01:04,104
Wes looks at you.

33
00:01:04,104 --> 00:01:05,577
Vera looks at the stairs,

34
00:01:05,577 --> 00:01:07,550
the way she looks at every door.

35
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:09,694
The rule is the boy's rule now,

36
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:13,012
the one Nora taught him on day 245.

37
00:01:13,644 --> 00:01:15,795
If somebody knocks any other way,

38
00:01:15,795 --> 00:01:17,107
you don't open.

39
00:01:17,722 --> 00:01:19,005
"We don't open at night,"

40
00:01:19,005 --> 00:01:20,663
you call up through the grille.

41
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:21,444
A pause.

42
00:01:21,803 --> 00:01:23,702
Then, surprisingly, a laugh.

43
00:01:23,702 --> 00:01:24,883
A tired one.

44
00:01:25,595 --> 00:01:26,980
"Good," says the woman.

45
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:28,225
"Neither do we."

46
00:01:29,274 --> 00:01:30,631
The beam clicks off.

47
00:01:30,631 --> 00:01:32,906
You hear boots, a few steps,

48
00:01:32,906 --> 00:01:35,221
and then the soft sound of people sitting down on

49
00:01:35,221 --> 00:01:37,840
the pavement on the other side of your gate,

50
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,767
as if they are ready to wait all night.

51
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:40,549
They are.

52
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,674
On day 272, at first light,

53
00:01:43,674 --> 00:01:46,609
Wes goes up to the gantry with his mirror.

54
00:01:46,609 --> 00:01:49,022
He comes back down two minutes later

55
00:01:49,022 --> 00:01:50,764
and describes them the way he used to

56
00:01:50,764 --> 00:01:53,470
describe the river, one thing at a time.

57
00:01:53,470 --> 00:01:54,510
"Three," he says.

58
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:56,926
"A woman in a yellow raincoat.

59
00:01:56,926 --> 00:01:57,772
Very yellow.

60
00:01:57,772 --> 00:02:00,220
You could see her from the moon.

61
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:01,087
A boy,

62
00:02:01,087 --> 00:02:04,330
maybe twelve, in a white bicycle helmet.

63
00:02:04,705 --> 00:02:06,037
And a big man with a blue

64
00:02:06,037 --> 00:02:07,370
and white checked blanket

65
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:09,725
round his shoulders, like a cape.

66
00:02:09,725 --> 00:02:11,588
He's asleep sitting up."

67
00:02:12,155 --> 00:02:13,641
Wes thinks about it.

68
00:02:13,641 --> 00:02:14,719
"Like Vera."

69
00:02:15,286 --> 00:02:18,468
"Nobody sleeps like me," says Vera.

70
00:02:18,468 --> 00:02:20,514
You go up and see for yourself.

71
00:02:20,514 --> 00:02:22,053
They are sitting with their

72
00:02:22,053 --> 00:02:24,321
backs against the wall across the street,

73
00:02:24,321 --> 00:02:25,766
right under the sign.

74
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:28,942
FOUR ALIVE, and the frequency.

75
00:02:28,942 --> 00:02:30,936
The woman in yellow sees your

76
00:02:30,936 --> 00:02:33,232
head over the gate and lifts one hand.

77
00:02:33,847 --> 00:02:34,453
Empty.

78
00:02:34,453 --> 00:02:37,002
"My name's Ruth," she says.

79
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:38,311
"That's Kit.

80
00:02:38,311 --> 00:02:40,258
The one snoring is Bram.

81
00:02:40,258 --> 00:02:41,767
We walked nineteen days

82
00:02:41,767 --> 00:02:43,531
to knock on that gate."

83
00:02:43,531 --> 00:02:43,915
"Why?"

84
00:02:43,915 --> 00:02:45,134
you ask.

85
00:02:45,134 --> 00:02:46,663
She points up at the sign.

86
00:02:46,663 --> 00:02:48,676
"Because somebody on that frequency

87
00:02:48,676 --> 00:02:51,669
says Still here every night," she says.

88
00:02:52,106 --> 00:02:53,065
"On a clear night,

89
00:02:53,065 --> 00:02:55,548
we can hear it all the way from the sea."

90
00:02:56,290 --> 00:02:57,199
Behind you,

91
00:02:57,199 --> 00:02:59,924
on the stairs, Nora stops dead.

92
00:03:00,377 --> 00:03:05,281
From day 273 to day 274,

93
00:03:05,655 --> 00:03:07,327
you talk through the gate.

94
00:03:07,327 --> 00:03:08,503
You don't open it.

95
00:03:08,503 --> 00:03:10,572
You carry the bench up into the yard,

96
00:03:10,572 --> 00:03:13,054
and they sit on their side of the bars,

97
00:03:13,054 --> 00:03:14,323
and you sit on yours,

98
00:03:14,323 --> 00:03:16,732
and it is the strangest conversation you

99
00:03:16,732 --> 00:03:18,091
have had since day one,

100
00:03:18,091 --> 00:03:21,456
because nobody is whispering and nobody is dead.

101
00:03:21,456 --> 00:03:23,917
At sunset, Ansel comes on the radio,

102
00:03:23,917 --> 00:03:26,000
the way he does every night.

103
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,909
"Pit's quiet.

104
00:03:26,909 --> 00:03:28,526
Bridge is ours."

105
00:03:28,526 --> 00:03:30,763
Then, "Did three people come your way?

106
00:03:30,763 --> 00:03:31,619
Yellow coat,

107
00:03:31,619 --> 00:03:34,283
white helmet, a big man in a blanket?"

108
00:03:34,283 --> 00:03:35,719
You look at the gate.

109
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:37,696
"They're sitting outside it."

110
00:03:37,696 --> 00:03:39,540
"They came through the city

111
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:41,561
eight days ago," says Ansel.

112
00:03:41,561 --> 00:03:43,238
"They asked about the depot.

113
00:03:43,238 --> 00:03:45,680
They mended the pump at our spring,

114
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,056
which nobody here could do.

115
00:03:47,056 --> 00:03:48,366
And the big one sings

116
00:03:48,366 --> 00:03:50,694
better than anyone on our bridge."

117
00:03:50,694 --> 00:03:51,610
A pause.

118
00:03:52,145 --> 00:03:53,722
"That isn't difficult."

119
00:03:53,722 --> 00:03:56,577
"Anybody can mend a pump," says Vera,

120
00:03:56,577 --> 00:03:58,280
when the radio is off.

121
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,719
"I can't," says Wes.

122
00:04:00,719 --> 00:04:03,769
On day 274, you ask Ruth the

123
00:04:03,769 --> 00:04:05,487
question that kept you awake.

124
00:04:05,487 --> 00:04:08,070
"Your torch went straight to our grille.

125
00:04:08,070 --> 00:04:09,693
How did you know where to look?"

126
00:04:09,693 --> 00:04:11,454
Ruth looks almost sorry.

127
00:04:11,454 --> 00:04:13,378
"Your lantern," she says.

128
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:14,757
"Every night,

129
00:04:14,757 --> 00:04:16,520
a little glow comes out of that grille,

130
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:18,312
right at the bottom of the wall.

131
00:04:18,846 --> 00:04:19,993
We watched it for three

132
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:21,485
nights before we knocked.

133
00:04:21,485 --> 00:04:23,312
It goes down when you sleep.

134
00:04:23,312 --> 00:04:24,805
It comes up again when

135
00:04:24,805 --> 00:04:26,792
somebody has a bad dream."

136
00:04:27,325 --> 00:04:29,519
Nobody says anything.

137
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:31,411
For two hundred and seventy days,

138
00:04:31,411 --> 00:04:33,982
you thought the dark was keeping you safe.

139
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,759
It turns out the dark had a

140
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:37,564
little light in it all along,

141
00:04:37,564 --> 00:04:39,781
and anybody could have seen it.

142
00:04:39,781 --> 00:04:42,148
That night, Wes tapes a square of

143
00:04:42,148 --> 00:04:44,739
cardboard over the inside of the grille.

144
00:04:44,739 --> 00:04:45,834
Neatly.

145
00:04:45,834 --> 00:04:46,872
Very neatly.

146
00:04:46,872 --> 00:04:50,410
"It's not personal," he tells the grille.

147
00:04:50,410 --> 00:04:53,294
On day 275, you open the gate.

148
00:04:53,294 --> 00:04:54,207
In daylight.

149
00:04:54,207 --> 00:04:55,682
That's the new rule,

150
00:04:55,682 --> 00:04:58,799
and you say it out loud, so it's been said.

151
00:04:58,799 --> 00:05:01,588
You open in daylight, or you don't open.

152
00:05:01,588 --> 00:05:03,212
Vera stands on the gantry with

153
00:05:03,212 --> 00:05:05,486
the rope of the bolt in her hand.

154
00:05:05,486 --> 00:05:07,769
Nora stands beside you with the flashlight,

155
00:05:07,769 --> 00:05:09,400
although it is noon.

156
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,548
Wes stands slightly behind everybody,

157
00:05:11,548 --> 00:05:13,046
oiling nothing.

158
00:05:13,046 --> 00:05:14,081
The bolt lifts.

159
00:05:14,081 --> 00:05:15,634
The gate whispers open.

160
00:05:15,634 --> 00:05:17,624
And three people walk into your yard,

161
00:05:17,624 --> 00:05:19,296
very slowly, the way you would

162
00:05:19,296 --> 00:05:21,318
walk into somebody else's kitchen.

163
00:05:21,318 --> 00:05:22,827
Kit looks at everything.

164
00:05:22,827 --> 00:05:23,730
The fire.

165
00:05:24,183 --> 00:05:25,501
The dark rectangle where

166
00:05:25,501 --> 00:05:26,819
the coach used to stand.

167
00:05:26,819 --> 00:05:29,044
The canopy, the solar panel,

168
00:05:29,044 --> 00:05:32,292
the loudspeaker with its switch taped on OFF.

169
00:05:32,292 --> 00:05:34,444
He looks at your yard as if it is a

170
00:05:34,444 --> 00:05:37,233
famous place he has read about in a book.

171
00:05:37,233 --> 00:05:38,462
Bram looks at the gate.

172
00:05:38,462 --> 00:05:40,547
Then he takes a small can of oil

173
00:05:40,547 --> 00:05:41,944
out from under his blanket and

174
00:05:41,944 --> 00:05:44,091
holds it out to Wes, without a word.

175
00:05:44,091 --> 00:05:45,313
Wes takes it.

176
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:47,261
"Finally," he says.

177
00:05:47,261 --> 00:05:49,487
"Somebody who understands."

178
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:51,683
Before anything else,

179
00:05:51,683 --> 00:05:53,660
Nora teaches them the knock.

180
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:54,793
Three times.

181
00:05:54,793 --> 00:05:56,496
Then a fourth time, softer.

182
00:05:56,496 --> 00:05:59,281
Ruth tries it on the gatepost twice,

183
00:05:59,281 --> 00:06:00,291
until she has it.

184
00:06:00,291 --> 00:06:02,638
"And yours," Nora says.

185
00:06:02,638 --> 00:06:03,013
"Two.

186
00:06:03,013 --> 00:06:03,763
Hard."

187
00:06:03,763 --> 00:06:06,010
"Two hard means we're alive

188
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:07,737
and we're asking," says Ruth.

189
00:06:07,737 --> 00:06:09,025
"Not telling.

190
00:06:09,025 --> 00:06:09,679
Asking."

191
00:06:09,679 --> 00:06:10,577
Nora nods.

192
00:06:10,577 --> 00:06:12,756
"Ours means we're home."

193
00:06:13,354 --> 00:06:17,277
From day 276 to day 278,

194
00:06:17,602 --> 00:06:19,755
Ruth tells you where they came from.

195
00:06:19,755 --> 00:06:22,869
They sit at your fire and eat the hill's potatoes,

196
00:06:22,869 --> 00:06:23,921
and Ruth draws it for

197
00:06:23,921 --> 00:06:25,921
you with a stick in the ash,

198
00:06:25,921 --> 00:06:28,904
the way Ansel drew the gravel pit in the frost.

199
00:06:28,904 --> 00:06:29,484
A coast.

200
00:06:29,484 --> 00:06:30,387
A long beach.

201
00:06:30,387 --> 00:06:32,673
And at the end of the beach,

202
00:06:32,673 --> 00:06:34,343
out in the sea, a rock with a

203
00:06:34,343 --> 00:06:36,646
little town on it, and a lighthouse.

204
00:06:37,084 --> 00:06:38,727
One road goes out to it,

205
00:06:38,727 --> 00:06:42,144
a long, low road of stone laid across the sand.

206
00:06:42,144 --> 00:06:44,040
"The Point," says Ruth.

207
00:06:44,382 --> 00:06:46,241
"That's what everybody calls it.

208
00:06:46,241 --> 00:06:48,007
Thirty-one of us live there.

209
00:06:48,007 --> 00:06:50,403
Kit's father keeps the lighthouse."

210
00:06:50,403 --> 00:06:52,848
"One road," says Vera, leaning in.

211
00:06:52,848 --> 00:06:54,771
"One road," says Ruth.

212
00:06:55,144 --> 00:06:56,256
"And twice a day,

213
00:06:56,256 --> 00:06:58,481
the sea comes in and covers it.

214
00:06:58,481 --> 00:06:59,743
For six hours,

215
00:06:59,743 --> 00:07:01,524
nothing can walk to the Point.

216
00:07:01,524 --> 00:07:01,984
Not us.

217
00:07:01,984 --> 00:07:02,859
Not them."

218
00:07:03,475 --> 00:07:05,247
She rubs the road out with her thumb.

219
00:07:05,247 --> 00:07:06,713
Then she draws it again.

220
00:07:07,264 --> 00:07:08,665
"Then the sea goes out,

221
00:07:08,665 --> 00:07:10,257
and the road comes back."

222
00:07:10,257 --> 00:07:13,415
Wes stares at the drawing for a long time.

223
00:07:13,415 --> 00:07:16,175
"A gate that closes itself," he says.

224
00:07:16,175 --> 00:07:17,920
"And opens itself."

225
00:07:18,423 --> 00:07:19,982
"Twice a day," says Ruth.

226
00:07:19,982 --> 00:07:21,581
"You get used to it."

227
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:22,753
"And them?"

228
00:07:22,753 --> 00:07:23,414
you ask.

229
00:07:23,414 --> 00:07:24,147
"The dead.

230
00:07:24,147 --> 00:07:26,032
Do they get used to it?"

231
00:07:26,032 --> 00:07:28,931
Ruth's face changes, just a little.

232
00:07:28,931 --> 00:07:31,172
"Some of them come along the

233
00:07:31,172 --> 00:07:32,763
beach at low tide," she says.

234
00:07:32,763 --> 00:07:33,889
"Not many.

235
00:07:33,889 --> 00:07:35,413
A few dozen every winter.

236
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:37,497
They walk out along the road until

237
00:07:37,497 --> 00:07:39,255
they reach our gate at the end of it,

238
00:07:39,255 --> 00:07:40,784
and they stand there with their

239
00:07:40,784 --> 00:07:43,328
hands on it, until the sea comes in and

240
00:07:43,328 --> 00:07:46,171
pushes them gently back to the beach."

241
00:07:46,171 --> 00:07:47,483
She shrugs.

242
00:07:47,921 --> 00:07:50,478
"Next low tide, they walk out again."

243
00:07:50,478 --> 00:07:52,848
"Like the Doorman," says Wes.

244
00:07:52,848 --> 00:07:54,374
"Who's the Doorman?"

245
00:07:54,374 --> 00:07:55,477
asks Kit.

246
00:07:55,803 --> 00:07:56,771
Wes tells him.

247
00:07:56,771 --> 00:07:58,965
It takes the rest of the evening.

248
00:07:58,965 --> 00:08:00,008
On day 277,

249
00:08:00,008 --> 00:08:02,866
you ask her the other question.

250
00:08:02,866 --> 00:08:04,849
Why walk nineteen days inland,

251
00:08:04,849 --> 00:08:08,155
past every empty town, to knock on one gate?

252
00:08:08,155 --> 00:08:09,731
Ruth looks at Nora.

253
00:08:09,731 --> 00:08:11,802
"We listen to the radio

254
00:08:11,802 --> 00:08:13,059
every night," she says.

255
00:08:13,059 --> 00:08:15,155
"For a long time, there was nothing.

256
00:08:15,155 --> 00:08:17,982
Then one winter, a woman's voice.

257
00:08:17,982 --> 00:08:18,988
Still here.

258
00:08:18,988 --> 00:08:20,077
Every night.

259
00:08:20,077 --> 00:08:22,842
Sometimes there were men with her,

260
00:08:22,842 --> 00:08:25,432
saying other things, about rivers and horns.

261
00:08:25,432 --> 00:08:28,058
But every single night, Still here."

262
00:08:28,058 --> 00:08:29,233
She shrugs.

263
00:08:29,912 --> 00:08:31,770
"Kit wanted to know who it was.

264
00:08:31,770 --> 00:08:32,669
So did I.

265
00:08:33,284 --> 00:08:34,910
When you spend a winter on a rock,

266
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:36,415
you start to need to know the

267
00:08:36,415 --> 00:08:38,509
rest of the world hasn't stopped."

268
00:08:38,509 --> 00:08:40,686
Nora doesn't say anything.

269
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:41,912
She looks at the fire.

270
00:08:41,912 --> 00:08:44,136
Then she gets up and walks away,

271
00:08:44,136 --> 00:08:46,415
very fast, toward the depot building.

272
00:08:46,415 --> 00:08:48,628
"Did I say something wrong?"

273
00:08:48,628 --> 00:08:49,587
Ruth asks.

274
00:08:49,587 --> 00:08:50,807
"No," says Wes.

275
00:08:50,807 --> 00:08:52,969
"You said something right.

276
00:08:52,969 --> 00:08:54,608
She's not used to it."

277
00:08:55,511 --> 00:08:59,527
On day 278, Bram fixes the drip over your bench,

278
00:08:59,527 --> 00:09:00,441
the one that has been

279
00:09:00,441 --> 00:09:02,747
dripping for as long as you can remember.

280
00:09:02,747 --> 00:09:03,632
He doesn't say a

281
00:09:03,632 --> 00:09:05,090
single word the whole time.

282
00:09:05,090 --> 00:09:06,341
When it's done,

283
00:09:06,341 --> 00:09:10,061
he whistles three notes, low, and goes back to the fire.

284
00:09:10,612 --> 00:09:12,024
"He whistles instead of

285
00:09:12,024 --> 00:09:13,967
talking," Kit explains.

286
00:09:13,967 --> 00:09:16,516
"Three notes means done."

287
00:09:16,516 --> 00:09:19,703
On day 279, Ruth sees the locker.

288
00:09:19,703 --> 00:09:21,782
Nora shows it to her herself.

289
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:24,666
The narrow room at the end of the depot,

290
00:09:24,666 --> 00:09:26,721
the row of tall metal lockers,

291
00:09:26,721 --> 00:09:28,769
the one door standing open.

292
00:09:28,769 --> 00:09:31,019
The folded cleaning jacket.

293
00:09:31,019 --> 00:09:32,005
The gloves.

294
00:09:32,005 --> 00:09:33,300
The road map,

295
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:36,208
with its pencil circle at the edge of the sea.

296
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:39,666
And the postcard, taped inside the door.

297
00:09:39,666 --> 00:09:40,712
Blue sea.

298
00:09:41,344 --> 00:09:42,306
Yellow sand.

299
00:09:42,306 --> 00:09:45,618
Ruth stands in front of it, very still.

300
00:09:45,618 --> 00:09:48,132
Then she reaches out and puts one

301
00:09:48,132 --> 00:09:50,624
finger on the corner of the postcard,

302
00:09:50,624 --> 00:09:52,840
where a tiny white tower stands on

303
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:55,131
a dark rock at the end of the beach.

304
00:09:55,714 --> 00:09:57,844
"That's our lighthouse," she says.

305
00:09:57,844 --> 00:09:59,048
Nobody moves.

306
00:09:59,662 --> 00:10:01,389
"That's the Point," says Ruth.

307
00:10:01,389 --> 00:10:02,461
"That's our beach.

308
00:10:02,461 --> 00:10:04,895
Somebody printed it on a card.

309
00:10:04,895 --> 00:10:07,260
I always wondered who bought them."

310
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,723
"Me," says Nora.

311
00:10:08,723 --> 00:10:10,562
Her voice is very small.

312
00:10:10,562 --> 00:10:11,451
"Before.

313
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:13,101
I bought it before.

314
00:10:13,101 --> 00:10:14,375
I was going to go."

315
00:10:14,375 --> 00:10:16,556
Behind her, Wes takes off his beanie.

316
00:10:16,556 --> 00:10:17,699
It is only the third time

317
00:10:17,699 --> 00:10:19,475
you have ever seen him do that.

318
00:10:19,475 --> 00:10:22,575
"That's the beach," he says quietly.

319
00:10:22,575 --> 00:10:23,877
"I promised."

320
00:10:23,877 --> 00:10:27,535
From day 280 to day 284,

321
00:10:27,535 --> 00:10:30,603
there are seven at the fire.

322
00:10:31,153 --> 00:10:33,741
It takes some getting used to.

323
00:10:33,741 --> 00:10:34,493
Seven bowls.

324
00:10:34,493 --> 00:10:36,096
Seven places on a bench that

325
00:10:36,096 --> 00:10:37,713
was only ever built for four.

326
00:10:38,211 --> 00:10:40,233
Kit tries to sleep on the canopy ladder,

327
00:10:40,233 --> 00:10:41,998
until Nora makes him come down.

328
00:10:41,998 --> 00:10:43,972
Bram sleeps sitting up against the

329
00:10:43,972 --> 00:10:46,487
gate with his blanket over his head,

330
00:10:46,487 --> 00:10:48,412
and Vera, who has slept sitting up for

331
00:10:48,412 --> 00:10:51,391
nearly a year, watches him do it with a look

332
00:10:51,391 --> 00:10:53,671
you have never seen on her face before.

333
00:10:54,013 --> 00:10:55,106
Respect, maybe.

334
00:10:55,106 --> 00:10:57,155
Wes takes the pencil and adds

335
00:10:57,155 --> 00:10:59,630
three marks to the people met column.

336
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:00,838
Then, after a moment,

337
00:11:00,838 --> 00:11:03,231
he hands the pencil to Kit.

338
00:11:03,231 --> 00:11:04,804
"Your turn," he says.

339
00:11:04,804 --> 00:11:05,654
"Do us."

340
00:11:06,268 --> 00:11:07,637
Kit adds four.

341
00:11:07,637 --> 00:11:10,909
On day 281, Kit stands under the

342
00:11:10,909 --> 00:11:13,098
canopy and points up at the loudspeaker,

343
00:11:13,098 --> 00:11:15,097
with its switch taped on OFF.

344
00:11:15,097 --> 00:11:16,352
"What's that for?"

345
00:11:16,352 --> 00:11:18,179
"Calling them," says Wes.

346
00:11:18,179 --> 00:11:19,320
"It's on the list of

347
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,989
things I'm sorry about."

348
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:22,498
"Does it still work?"

349
00:11:22,498 --> 00:11:24,395
Wes looks up at the solar panel,

350
00:11:24,395 --> 00:11:25,558
shining in the sun,

351
00:11:25,558 --> 00:11:28,300
the way it has every day since you met him.

352
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:30,924
"The battery's full," he says.

353
00:11:30,924 --> 00:11:32,724
"That's the problem with it."

354
00:11:32,724 --> 00:11:37,030
On day 282, the hill people come down with apples,

355
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,138
and the boy with the blue

356
00:11:38,138 --> 00:11:40,565
bandage meets the boy in the white helmet.

357
00:11:40,565 --> 00:11:43,333
They stare at each other for a full minute,

358
00:11:43,333 --> 00:11:44,653
two very serious faces,

359
00:11:44,653 --> 00:11:46,698
like two dogs meeting in a park.

360
00:11:46,698 --> 00:11:49,773
Then the hill boy teaches Kit the horn code,

361
00:11:49,773 --> 00:11:50,839
and Kit teaches the hill

362
00:11:50,839 --> 00:11:52,125
boy to knock twice,

363
00:11:52,125 --> 00:11:55,257
hard, and by evening they have invented a third knock

364
00:11:55,257 --> 00:11:58,711
that nobody else is allowed to know.

365
00:11:58,711 --> 00:12:00,225
Every sunset,

366
00:12:00,225 --> 00:12:03,286
Nora says Still here into the radio.

367
00:12:03,286 --> 00:12:05,521
Now she knows that somebody on a

368
00:12:05,521 --> 00:12:07,508
rock by the sea might be listening,

369
00:12:07,508 --> 00:12:09,255
and she says it a little slower,

370
00:12:09,255 --> 00:12:11,513
as if she wants it to arrive safely.

371
00:12:11,935 --> 00:12:16,091
From day 285 to day 287,

372
00:12:16,091 --> 00:12:16,914
Ruth asks.

373
00:12:16,914 --> 00:12:19,864
She waits until the fire is low,

374
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:23,022
on day 285, and everybody is there.

375
00:12:23,557 --> 00:12:25,517
"Come with us," she says.

376
00:12:25,517 --> 00:12:26,660
"To the Point.

377
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,806
All four of you.

378
00:12:27,806 --> 00:12:28,912
There's room.

379
00:12:28,912 --> 00:12:30,255
There are boats.

380
00:12:30,255 --> 00:12:31,661
There's fish.

381
00:12:32,003 --> 00:12:34,551
And a gate the dead can't open."

382
00:12:34,551 --> 00:12:36,125
Nobody answers.

383
00:12:36,483 --> 00:12:37,797
You knew it was coming.

384
00:12:37,797 --> 00:12:40,123
You still have nothing ready to say.

385
00:12:40,657 --> 00:12:42,236
"Two days' drive," says Ruth,

386
00:12:42,236 --> 00:12:43,815
"when the roads are clear.

387
00:12:43,815 --> 00:12:45,616
You've got a truck.

388
00:12:45,616 --> 00:12:47,151
You've got a driver."

389
00:12:47,151 --> 00:12:48,539
She looks at Vera.

390
00:12:48,539 --> 00:12:51,808
"I hear you've got a very good driver."

391
00:12:51,808 --> 00:12:54,640
Vera turns a stick over in the fire.

392
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,800
"One way in," she says.

393
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,439
"And the sea for a gate."

394
00:12:58,439 --> 00:13:00,037
She almost smiles.

395
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:02,035
"My favorite kind."

396
00:13:02,035 --> 00:13:03,580
Nora looks at you.

397
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:05,499
And you understand that she

398
00:13:05,499 --> 00:13:07,547
isn't asking you whether to go.

399
00:13:07,857 --> 00:13:09,268
She has been going since the

400
00:13:09,268 --> 00:13:11,242
day she bought that postcard.

401
00:13:11,242 --> 00:13:13,310
She is asking you if you are coming.

402
00:13:13,310 --> 00:13:14,540
You look at the gate.

403
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:16,136
At the bunker door.

404
00:13:16,136 --> 00:13:17,709
At the yard you lived under,

405
00:13:17,709 --> 00:13:20,527
then took back, then made your own.

406
00:13:20,527 --> 00:13:21,435
Two hundred and eighty-five days,

407
00:13:21,435 --> 00:13:24,758
and you have never had to decide to leave.

408
00:13:24,758 --> 00:13:26,571
Leaving was always something

409
00:13:26,571 --> 00:13:29,034
that happened to other people.

410
00:13:29,034 --> 00:13:32,130
"When the roads are clear," you say.

411
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:33,616
It isn't a yes.

412
00:13:33,616 --> 00:13:35,920
Nora knows it isn't a yes.

413
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,627
But she smiles anyway,

414
00:13:37,627 --> 00:13:41,280
as if it's the first half of one.

415
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:43,900
On day 287, Wes starts a list

416
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:45,803
on the wall, beside the chart.

417
00:13:45,803 --> 00:13:47,472
Things we'd take.

418
00:13:47,472 --> 00:13:50,425
The first thing on it is the orange bag.

419
00:13:50,425 --> 00:13:53,297
From day 288 to day 295,

420
00:13:53,297 --> 00:13:54,652
it rains.

421
00:13:54,652 --> 00:13:56,307
Not snow.

422
00:13:56,735 --> 00:13:57,584
Not sleet.

423
00:13:57,584 --> 00:14:00,741
Rain, the first real rain of spring,

424
00:14:01,146 --> 00:14:03,249
warm and heavy and endless.

425
00:14:03,249 --> 00:14:05,073
It drums on the canopy

426
00:14:05,073 --> 00:14:06,710
the way the river used to.

427
00:14:06,710 --> 00:14:08,455
It fills the dark rectangle

428
00:14:08,455 --> 00:14:10,644
in the yard until it is a pond.

429
00:14:10,644 --> 00:14:12,302
It finds its way around the

430
00:14:12,302 --> 00:14:14,082
cardboard on the grille and runs down

431
00:14:14,082 --> 00:14:15,428
the bunker wall,

432
00:14:15,428 --> 00:14:17,947
and Bram stands under it for a long time with his

433
00:14:17,947 --> 00:14:20,323
hand flat on the concrete, listening.

434
00:14:20,323 --> 00:14:22,144
Then he whistles two notes,

435
00:14:22,144 --> 00:14:24,964
which Kit says means not good.

436
00:14:24,964 --> 00:14:26,392
On day 290,

437
00:14:26,392 --> 00:14:28,760
Ansel's voice on the radio changes.

438
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,811
"Pit's quiet," he says.

439
00:14:30,811 --> 00:14:32,950
Then, "Pit's wet."

440
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:36,326
On day 292, he says, "Pit's filling."

441
00:14:36,326 --> 00:14:38,583
You stand on the bunker stairs

442
00:14:38,583 --> 00:14:40,209
with the radio, and you can see

443
00:14:40,209 --> 00:14:42,381
it as if you were up on the rim.

444
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:43,627
The frozen puddle at the

445
00:14:43,627 --> 00:14:44,923
bottom of the gravel pit,

446
00:14:44,923 --> 00:14:47,158
the one the size of a car park, growing.

447
00:14:47,158 --> 00:14:48,061
Spreading.

448
00:14:48,370 --> 00:14:50,383
Rising around the wheels of the coach.

449
00:14:50,383 --> 00:14:51,725
And thousands of the dead

450
00:14:51,725 --> 00:14:53,883
standing in it, perfectly still,

451
00:14:53,883 --> 00:14:56,920
facing a bus with nothing left to say,

452
00:14:56,920 --> 00:14:59,327
while the water climbs past their knees.

453
00:14:59,927 --> 00:15:02,467
"They don't seem to notice," says Ansel.

454
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:05,320
"They're just standing in it."

455
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,449
On day 294,

456
00:15:06,449 --> 00:15:10,390
he says, "It's up to their waists."

457
00:15:10,390 --> 00:15:13,727
On day 295, the rain stops.

458
00:15:13,727 --> 00:15:17,192
From day 296 to day 299,

459
00:15:17,192 --> 00:15:19,469
the world dries out.

460
00:15:19,469 --> 00:15:21,458
The yard steams in the sun.

461
00:15:21,458 --> 00:15:24,572
The pond in the rectangle shrinks back.

462
00:15:24,572 --> 00:15:26,326
Bram climbs onto the canopy and

463
00:15:26,326 --> 00:15:27,945
clears the gutter,

464
00:15:27,945 --> 00:15:30,912
Kit hands him things, and Wes supervises,

465
00:15:30,912 --> 00:15:34,657
which mostly means sitting on the ladder.

466
00:15:34,657 --> 00:15:37,486
On day 297, Ruth takes the road map

467
00:15:37,486 --> 00:15:39,978
down from the locker and draws the way home

468
00:15:39,978 --> 00:15:42,341
on it in pencil, a thin line from the

469
00:15:42,341 --> 00:15:45,489
edge of the city to the circle by the sea.

470
00:15:45,489 --> 00:15:46,140
Two days.

471
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:47,711
Back roads.

472
00:15:47,711 --> 00:15:49,952
One bridge she isn't sure about.

473
00:15:49,952 --> 00:15:52,493
"When the roads are clear," she says,

474
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,207
and folds it up again.

475
00:15:54,207 --> 00:15:57,664
Nora pins it back in the locker beside the postcard,

476
00:15:57,664 --> 00:15:58,898
and for the first time,

477
00:15:58,898 --> 00:16:01,639
you notice she has left room next to them.

478
00:16:01,639 --> 00:16:04,621
As if something else is going to go there.

479
00:16:04,621 --> 00:16:07,903
On day 298, you go down to the bunker

480
00:16:07,903 --> 00:16:10,560
alone and stand in front of the chart.

481
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:11,177
Days.

482
00:16:11,177 --> 00:16:12,618
Zombies gone.

483
00:16:12,618 --> 00:16:14,153
People met.

484
00:16:14,511 --> 00:16:15,943
Days in daylight.

485
00:16:15,943 --> 00:16:18,153
Wes's list beside them.

486
00:16:18,527 --> 00:16:20,551
You put your hand flat on the wall,

487
00:16:20,551 --> 00:16:22,988
the way Bram listens to concrete,

488
00:16:22,988 --> 00:16:26,436
and you try to imagine the room without anybody in it.

489
00:16:26,436 --> 00:16:27,978
The lantern cold.

490
00:16:27,978 --> 00:16:29,735
The bench empty.

491
00:16:30,109 --> 00:16:32,883
The door open, with nobody behind it.

492
00:16:32,883 --> 00:16:34,008
You can't.

493
00:16:34,527 --> 00:16:35,694
You have tried before.

494
00:16:35,694 --> 00:16:36,760
It always turns into

495
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,542
the first night instead.

496
00:16:38,542 --> 00:16:39,134
The stairs.

497
00:16:39,134 --> 00:16:39,924
The steel door.

498
00:16:39,924 --> 00:16:42,050
The sound of the ceiling filling up.

499
00:16:42,456 --> 00:16:45,563
Every sunset, Ansel says, "Pit's quiet."

500
00:16:46,065 --> 00:16:48,899
Every sunset, Nora says, "Still here."

501
00:16:49,850 --> 00:16:52,532
On day 300, the radio is silent.

502
00:16:52,532 --> 00:16:54,203
Sunset comes and goes.

503
00:16:54,203 --> 00:16:55,543
Nora sits on the bench

504
00:16:55,543 --> 00:16:57,416
with the radio in her lap.

505
00:16:57,726 --> 00:16:59,513
Seven people around the fire,

506
00:16:59,513 --> 00:17:02,733
not talking, all listening to nothing.

507
00:17:02,733 --> 00:17:04,269
Ansel has not missed

508
00:17:04,269 --> 00:17:06,543
one evening since day 241.

509
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:08,355
It is properly dark when

510
00:17:08,355 --> 00:17:09,947
the radio finally crackles.

511
00:17:09,947 --> 00:17:13,106
And the voice that comes out of it is Ansel's,

512
00:17:13,106 --> 00:17:14,989
but he is whispering again.

513
00:17:15,508 --> 00:17:17,793
The way the whole city whispered for a

514
00:17:17,793 --> 00:17:20,720
month under a bridge full of the dead.

515
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:22,143
"Depot," he says.

516
00:17:22,143 --> 00:17:23,065
"Depot.

517
00:17:23,391 --> 00:17:24,525
Do you read?"

518
00:17:24,525 --> 00:17:26,919
"We read you," says Nora.

519
00:17:27,325 --> 00:17:29,735
"The wall came down," says Ansel.

520
00:17:29,735 --> 00:17:30,790
Nobody moves.

521
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:31,948
"The rain did it.

522
00:17:31,948 --> 00:17:33,977
A whole side of the pit just slid.

523
00:17:33,977 --> 00:17:35,719
It isn't a wall anymore.

524
00:17:35,719 --> 00:17:36,813
It's a slope.

525
00:17:36,813 --> 00:17:38,564
Mud, all the way from

526
00:17:38,564 --> 00:17:40,140
the bottom to the top.

527
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,674
A second way out."

528
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:43,952
You think of the gravel pit.

529
00:17:43,952 --> 00:17:44,955
The steep walls.

530
00:17:44,955 --> 00:17:46,377
The one road down.

531
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:48,409
A place with one way out.

532
00:17:48,409 --> 00:17:51,224
You think of the rule you were so sure of.

533
00:17:51,224 --> 00:17:52,701
They do not climb.

534
00:17:52,701 --> 00:17:54,457
They don't have to.

535
00:17:54,457 --> 00:17:56,058
Not anymore.

536
00:17:57,011 --> 00:17:58,597
Vera is already standing.

537
00:17:58,597 --> 00:18:00,882
She has her scarf in both hands,

538
00:18:00,882 --> 00:18:04,641
and her face is the face she had on day 241,

539
00:18:04,641 --> 00:18:06,687
when the radio asked for the driver.

540
00:18:06,687 --> 00:18:08,337
"Where are they going?"

541
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:09,508
she says.

542
00:18:09,508 --> 00:18:10,562
"Exactly."

543
00:18:10,562 --> 00:18:13,889
Ansel takes a long time to answer.

544
00:18:13,889 --> 00:18:16,169
"They're walking up it," he says.

545
00:18:16,169 --> 00:18:17,014
"All of them.

546
00:18:17,014 --> 00:18:19,787
Out of the pit and across the fields."

547
00:18:20,226 --> 00:18:21,273
A long breath.

548
00:18:21,273 --> 00:18:22,759
"Toward the city."

549
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,560
Then the radio clicks off.

550
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,909
Three hundred days.

551
00:18:26,909 --> 00:18:28,472
The same orange bandage.

552
00:18:28,472 --> 00:18:29,723
Nora is holding the

553
00:18:29,723 --> 00:18:31,463
flashlight and the radio.

554
00:18:31,463 --> 00:18:33,940
You are holding the orange bag.

555
00:18:34,298 --> 00:18:36,081
Tomorrow is day 301.

556
00:18:36,081 --> 00:18:38,917
Seven people are sitting around your fire,

557
00:18:38,917 --> 00:18:41,446
